{% set local_problem %}
<p><a href="/recent-projects/">Monrovia's</a> clay soil creates drainage challenges. Water doesn't absorb well, so it sits on the surface — or finds its way toward your foundation. Surface extensions help a little, but they only move water a few feet before releasing it onto that same uncooperative soil.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve this by routing water through buried pipes to controlled discharge points. The water exits far from your foundation, where it can't cause problems even on clay soil that won't absorb it.</p>

<p>For Monrovia homes with wet basements, foundation concerns, or persistent pooling, underground drains are often the only permanent solution.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes connecting downspouts to discharge points far from your home. Water flows through sealed channels to pop-up emitters, storm drains, or daylight exits at the property edge.</p>

<p>We design systems for your specific property — routing around obstacles, matching terrain, and choosing discharge points that make sense for your situation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been installing underground drainage in <a href="/recent-projects/">western Madison County</a> for over 20 years. We understand clay soil, local terrain, and what it takes to solve drainage problems permanently.</p>

<p>Our systems last decades. Quality materials, proper installation, and thoughtful design.</p>
{% endset %}
